    "body": "<!-- markdownlint-disable -->\n\n## Overview\n\nDeepGEMM's extension gets built by setuptools, which never sees `CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_LAUNCHER`. So it's the one file in the build that skips ccache/sccache. This passes the launcher through.\n\n## Claims\n\n- If you build with ccache or sccache, rebuilding `_deep_gemm_C` is a cache hit now instead of a ~60 s compile.\n- No launcher, no change.\n\n## Validation\n\n- A test extension built twice with `CC=\"ccache cc\"`: miss, then hit.\n- On a B200 box with a warm ccache and a fresh build dir, `_deep_gemm_C` took 65.7 s and was the last job ninja waited on. Will post the after number here, that's why it's a draft.\n\n## Details\n\n`build_deepgemm_C.py` now takes `--launcher` and sticks it in front of `CC`/`CXX`. `deepgemm.cmake` passes `CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_LAUNCHER` to it.\n\nI did it here instead of moving DeepGEMM to torch's `BuildExtension` so it uses whatever launcher vLLM picked (torch's own wrapper prefers ccache over sccache).\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
